   "item_id": 269081,
   "item_text": "1",
   "item_forum_id": 0,
   "item_type": "post",
   "in_feed": null,
   "is_watched": null,
   "item_score": "991",
   "id": "27474",
   "item_level": "991",
   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 269081,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 42552,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "We choose 5 points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/429755e67892d17b251ad758840515a89e64492b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" > on a circumference of radius 1 and centre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c79ddff6b45c6ad853d03d6231fdf0fba5ededb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O.$\"  width=\"18\" height=\"12\" > <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > is a point inside the circle. Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ef6fb9bb3f4c7cde39e9fe8ef9cd72dddbc484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"19\" height=\"16\" > as the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d3e171d8e75de731504e46d0698115fe355a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_iA_{i+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833e63ada00d4a8662c24b9439c6c95b49ac891b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{i+1}P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" >,</span> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/d/b9d568d353955fe66dfaaaa0bfd63303b73cc46b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_7 = A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204c808e9bb1e78eb500776f7baf6e17d827d01d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_6 = A_1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" > Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d3204adb4e378ee5f5007055be7cd4b2819faa85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OQ_i = d_i, i = 1,2, \\ldots, 5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"191\" height=\"16\" > Find the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83f30f245a3ddee9730cdf7be3be546881ffc43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod^5_{i=1} A_iQ_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"64\" height=\"50\" > in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b858ddffc19b159e753e01be8bd3801303510d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" >",
    "post_canonical": "We choose 5 points $A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_5$ on a circumference of radius 1 and centre $O.$ $P$ is a point inside the circle. Denote $Q_i$ as the intersection of $A_iA_{i+2}$ and $A_{i+1}P$, where $A_7 = A_2$ and $A_6 = A_1.$ Let $OQ_i = d_i, i = 1,2, \\ldots, 5.$ Find the product $\\prod^5_{i=1} A_iQ_i$ in terms of $d_i.$",
    "username": "orl",
    "post_number": 1,
    "post_format": "bbcode",
    "category_name": "High School Olympiads",
    "category_id": 6,
    "poster_avatar": "//avatar.artofproblemsolving.com/avatar_1991.jpg"
   }
