    "post_rendered": "Let's note that our sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" > satisfies: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d2339c9999fc2081f7ee526f3e1f182ebb353ddf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=f(n-k-1)f(k)+f(n-k)f(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"350\" height=\"18\" > (it can be checked by induction).<br>\nWe know that there doesn't exist such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e94c7c5659301fe5cea57db49f2616ec9aaf6cd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f20ee6c59fa33eed786e7e0a15be1dc95b3dac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(m,f(n+1))&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" > for any <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e2a79c07170b3fce337ad97aa42921d824b84a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in N-\\{1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" >,</span> because going backwards recurentially we would obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cda332a2ba5fb98baaf778340f470983cc70dd43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;gcd(m,f(1))=gcd(m,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"18\" > what's false.<br>\nFor every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f298e27f80655a6ad0bd1239d8ad0f0e9da41eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" > there exists the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531ba340396c936cb4833fff13400b5d81768981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0 \\in N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b6e8fcdca91467cd806e6f9aca99afb60b78b0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(k_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" >.</span> Let's proove that<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e94c7c5659301fe5cea57db49f2616ec9aaf6cd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" > if and only if <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/990a5af6ee47f8adf0e5500469fd66b5f0cdbdeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0|n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" >.</span> Let's assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c45a9440a903bd7c6cff6b0be3105608f3cd9e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" > because for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b5800f5ad040d308609190ef18a9e0ca08a9b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" > there is nothing to proove.<br>\nSuppose there exists such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ed27b8b4776c8e1f6b7bdc58ab33adf6b0fa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t \\in N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" > that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9b9279ced681e2c8674daf429038a3579e4b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" > doesn't divide <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\"  width=\"6\" height=\"11\" >.</span><br>\nThus we have: <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a830ab64c0ef28adafd75d000abf90c06e6cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(t)=&gt;m|f(t-k_0-1)f(k_0)+f(t-k_0)f(k_0+1)=&gt;m|f(t-k_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"550\" height=\"18\" >,</span> cause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"8\" > satisfies <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c7e6838949ed3a25e8efcbb31a8f1591ed874a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(m,f(k_0+1))=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" >-</span>what we have already mentioned. So if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f9b9279ced681e2c8674daf429038a3579e4b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" > then <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f2798a83027eb8c6d8d417675585f6ae0842a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(t-k_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" >.</span> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\"  width=\"6\" height=\"11\" > is not divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" > then there exists such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" > : <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5cacadeebad0c1150a3d2886ab09196896f72a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" > that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c5a520733d24ef0b524b83ea639006299a291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;t-ik_0&lt;k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" >,</span> so we received a number <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a309abcea83e3ac90a85ee9899ab83f27adb313.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t-ik_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" >,</span> which is smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" ><br>\nand satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c71cdb6f6710c9cd76daa89972a7bff5c215016.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(t-ik_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" > - we have a contradiction.<br>\nThus we proved that for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f298e27f80655a6ad0bd1239d8ad0f0e9da41eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" > there exists such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531ba340396c936cb4833fff13400b5d81768981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0 \\in N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" > that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e94c7c5659301fe5cea57db49f2616ec9aaf6cd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" > if and only if <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/0/990a5af6ee47f8adf0e5500469fd66b5f0cdbdeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0|n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" >.</span><br>\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f544648cc8345cb6c7e20e7efd8fc8ec563116ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m|f(f(n))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" > if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/87724bf53842f6f3ba3584a2240dc066b59364d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0|f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" > if and only if <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/73527fcbebeba6172708811d694855f6bc61a74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1|n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" >.</span> So our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\"  width=\"9\" height=\"12\" > satisfies: <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93abd17e2b17ed80b69c5fac5e9fb3af2c36499b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=k_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Let's note that our sequence $f(n)$ satisfies: $f(n)=f(n-k-1)f(k)+f(n-k)f(k+1)$ (it can be checked by induction). \r\nWe know that there doesn't exist such $n$ that $m|f(n)$ and $gcd(m,f(n+1))>1$ for any $m \\in N-\\{1\\}$, because going backwards recurentially we would obtain $1<gcd(m,f(1))=gcd(m,1)$ what's false.\r\nFor every $m \\in N$ there exists the smallest $k_0 \\in N$ such that $m|f(k_0)$. Let's proove that\r\n$m|f(n)$ if and only if $k_0|n$. Let's assume that $m>1$ because for $m=1$ there is nothing to proove.\r\nSuppose there exists such $t \\in N$ that $m|f(t)$ and $k_0$ doesn't divide $t$.\r\nThus we have: $m|f(t)=>m|f(t-k_0-1)f(k_0)+f(t-k_0)f(k_0+1)=>m|f(t-k_0)$, cause $m$ satisfies $gcd(m,f(k_0+1))=1$-what we have already mentioned. So if $m|f(t)$ then $m|f(t-k_0)$. Because $t$ is not divisible by $k_0$ then there exists such $i$ : $i \\geq 0$ that $0<t-ik_0<k_0$, so we received a number $t-ik_0$, which is smaller than $k_0$\r\nand satisfies $m|f(t-ik_0)$ - we have a contradiction.\r\nThus we proved that for every $m \\in N$ there exists such $k_0 \\in N$ that: $m|f(n)$ if and only if $k_0|n$. \r\nSo $m|f(f(n))$ if and only if $k_0|f(n)$ if and only if $k_1|n$. So our $d$ satisfies: $d=k_1$.",
